<title>FRANCE: Remy-Cointreau 1996/97 H1 profit falls.</title>
<headline>Remy-Cointreau 1996/97 H1 profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax attributable	    profit    41  vs  profit   215</p>
<p>    Pre-tax pre-exceptional	   loss     1  vs    loss    39</p>
<p>    Exceptional			   gain    44  vs    gain   257</p>
<p>    Financial result		    loss   211  vs    loss   255</p>
<p>    Operating			   profit   210  vs  profit   216</p>
<p>    Turnover				     3,066  vs	   2,941</p>
<p>NOTE - French drinks group Remy-Cointreau issued the results in a statement and said that, as customary, they are adjusted for seasonality.</p>
<p>Turnover rose four percent in the first half to September 30 on a three percent increase in volumes sold.</p>
<p>Operating profit fell three percent to 210 million francs, reflecting a 60 million franc increase in promotional expenses to develop Remy-Cointreau brands.</p>
<p>The financial result improved by 44 million francs, helped by a reduction in debt which brought the pre-tax, pre-exceptional result almost to breakeven.</p>
<p>The exceptional items are due essentially to the restructuring of part of the debt, it said in the statement.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
